    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 38.333, 517.557, 293.667, 595.89 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The proposed step-equilibration approach is based on the principle that only the finite element(s) with the switch point(s) have non-uniform discretization [ t l − 1 ,t l ]. The approach uses an indicator variable ( η ) for the switch point(s), which is determined by calculating and multiplying the sum of the complementarity variables in two consecutive finite elements."
