    "bounding box" : [ 38.333, 71.223, 293.667, 159.89 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "As mentioned in (10), the Nurkanovic formulation augments an additional [2 N { ˆ λ, ˆ ν } +(2 N − 2) { π λ ,π ν } +( N − 1) { τ } + ( N − 1) { η } ] variables and [2 N { (10a) } + (2 N − 2) { (10b) } +2( N − 1) { (10c) } +( N − 1) { (10d) } ] constraints for each complementarity constraint. This effectively decreases the degrees of freedom by N − 1 to that of the original problem and avoids non-unique solutions for the step size variables h i ."
  }, {
